  "reason": "R3 supplies essentially the same high-energy ball-milling-in-argon plus SPS route for a closely related equiatomic Cr-Fe-Ni-containing HEA, while R10 applies the same route directly to the CoCrFeNi base system with a 10-minute SPS hold. R6 further connects SPS-processed Co-Cr-Fe-Ni alloys containing Ti to FCC/BCC phase constitution and hardness. The remaining relevant records collectively establish equiatomic solid-solution formation, lattice-distortion/solid-solution hardening, grain-size strengthening, dislocation-mediated behavior, and the strength–ductility consequences of hard or dual phases. Thus an expert could plausibly combine the disclosed powder-processing route with Ti-bearing CoCrFeNi chemistry and anticipate a dense, fine-grained FCC/BCC high-hardness alloy, although the exact 83/17 phase ratio and reported numerical properties would not be predictable."
